        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.33,
          "end": 17.3,
          "en": "And later on in upcoming sessions we'll be talking about the technical parts and how to work with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 17.33,
          "end": 18.83,
          "en": "Now what is broadcasting?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.83,
          "end": 25.76,
          "en": "Broadcasting in Laravel allows you to broadcast events from your server to connected clients like browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 25.76,
          "end": 30.83,
          "en": "mobile devices, etc. in real time using technologies like WebSocket.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 30.95,
          "end": 38,
          "en": "This is particularly useful for building real time features like notification, real time chat applications,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 38,
          "end": 39.47,
          "en": "live updates, etc..",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 39.47,
          "end": 40.76,
          "en": "So moral of the story?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 40.76,
          "end": 46.64,
          "en": "Whenever you have to work with some sort of real time communication stuff, will be using broadcasting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 47.3,
          "end": 51.29,
          "en": "Okay, let's say you are creating a chatting system, live chatting system.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 51.29,
          "end": 53.87,
          "en": "In that case, you have to use broadcasting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 54.05,
          "end": 57.62,
          "en": "Uh, suppose you are using WhatsApp or Facebook Messenger.",
          "zh": ""
        },
